{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchStrategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A strategy flushes the pending elements as one array in either of two ways: when an element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrives, by returning "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/flushes(pending:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or on events of its own (a timer, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signal), by calling "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchFlusher\/flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/run(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". After every flush, whatever its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cause, each strategy starts over. A flush with nothing pending emits nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The built-in strategies are "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CountBatchStrategy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/TimeBatchStrategy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (over a sequence or a unit of work) and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/EitherBatchStrategy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spelled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".count(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".time(interval:clock:tolerance:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".signal(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".either(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where a strategy is expected."}]},{"code":["\/\/ Up to 100 events per upload, and at least one upload every 5 seconds while events arrive.","let events = analyticsEvents.batch(strategy: .either(","    .count(100),","    .time(interval: .seconds(5), clock: ContinuousClock())))","for try await batch in events {","    try await upload(batch)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Writing a strategy","anchor":"Writing-a-strategy","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conform a type to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" and implement either requirement, or both; each has a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default that never flushes. Implement "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/flushes(pending:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to decide from the pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, after each one arrives. Implement "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/run(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to flush on events of your own: it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs in a task of its own while the batched sequence is iterated, and is cancelled when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batched sequence ends. A custom strategy composes with the built-in ones in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".either(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" is the batched sequence’s element: name it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flushes(pending:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or make the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"strategy generic over it when only "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/run(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" matters."}]},{"code":["\/\/\/ Flushes after each line, so every batch ends at a line break.","struct LineBatchStrategy: BatchStrategy {","    func flushes(pending: [Character]) -> Bool {","        pending.last == \"\\n\"","    }","}","","\/\/ A batch per line, or whatever has arrived after a second without one.","let lines = characters.batch(strategy: .either(","    LineBatchStrategy(),","    .time(interval: .seconds(1), clock: ContinuousClock())))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Batching needs iOS 16, Mac Catalyst 16, macOS 13, tvOS 16, watchOS 9 or visionOS 1."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"BatchStrategy.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/BatchStrategy.swift#L56"},"symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchStrategy"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","platforms":[{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false,"name":"iOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":